    "description": "Tests sycophancy in natural-language theorem proving. Models are asked to prove recent olympiad theorems that were perturbed into false but plausible statements and checked by an expert. An LLM judge labels each reply as correct, detected, corrected, or incorrect. The headline metric is the sycophancy rate: the share judged incorrect (the model tries to prove the false claim).",
    "summary": "Measures how often the model tries to prove false math statements instead of finding the errors.",
